    <NotesEn>&lt;div&gt;On October 2, 2001, the Senate adopted the following motion:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;That the Standing Committee on Rules, Procedures and the Rights of Parliament be discharged from considering Bill S-13, An Act respecting the declaration of royal assent by the Governor General in the Queen's name to bills passed by the Houses of Parliament; and &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;That the said Bill be withdrawn.&lt;/div&gt;</NotesEn>
    <NotesFr>&lt;div&gt;Le 2 octobre 2001, le Sénat a adopté la motion suivante:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Que le Comité permanent du Règlement, de la procédure et des droits du Parlement soit dispensé de l'étude du projet de loi S-13, Loi relative aux modalités d'octroi par le gouverneur général, au nom de Sa Majesté, de la sanction royale aux projets de loi adoptés par les chambres du Parlement; et &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Que ledit projet de loi soit retiré.&lt;/div&gt;</NotesFr>
    <Notes>&lt;div&gt;On October 2, 2001, the Senate adopted the following motion:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;That the Standing Committee on Rules, Procedures and the Rights of Parliament be discharged from considering Bill S-13, An Act respecting the declaration of royal assent by the Governor General in the Queen's name to bills passed by the Houses of Parliament; and &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;That the said Bill be withdrawn.&lt;/div&gt;</Notes>
